WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.939 --> 00:00:15.325
Last Thursday, just before dinner, Steve Jones and his sister were playing in their front yard.

2
00:00:16.026 --> 00:00:20.910
It was a warm spring day and they were enjoying themselves in the sun.

3
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.933
All of a sudden, the sky started to get dark.

4
00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:27.636
Then it became even darker.

5
00:00:29.088 --> 00:00:31.769
"It looks like it's going to rain," said Steve.

6
00:00:31.789 --> 00:00:33.610
"We'd better get inside."

7
00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:37.612
Just then the wind really started to blow.

8
00:00:38.312 --> 00:00:43.494
As the children reached their house, a large lightning bolt struck nearby.

9
00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:46.375
Then they heard thunder boom.

10
00:00:47.716 --> 00:00:50.537
Within minutes it was raining very hard.

11
00:00:50.557 --> 00:00:53.818
"This is the biggest thunderstorm I have ever seen!"

12
00:00:54.338 --> 00:00:55.639
exclaimed Steve.

13
00:00:55.659 --> 00:00:57.920
"Look! Now it's snowing!"

14
00:00:58.684 --> 00:01:01.545
"That's not snow," said Steve's dad.

15
00:01:01.565 --> 00:01:03.106
"That's hail.

16
00:01:03.366 --> 00:01:05.087
We'd better turn on the radio.

17
00:01:05.527 --> 00:01:07.328
There might be a tornado coming."

18
00:01:09.048 --> 00:01:15.811
"The National Weather Service has issued a tornado warning for Madison County in Texas," said the voice on

19
00:01:15.831 --> 00:01:16.491
the radio.

20
00:01:16.511 --> 00:01:19.112
"This could really be a bad one.

21
00:01:19.693 --> 00:01:24.354
You'd better move to a small room in your house and get away from any windows.

22
00:01:24.895 --> 00:01:27.936
If you have a basement, go downstairs right now."

23
00:01:29.372 --> 00:01:30.533
Then came the wind.

24
00:01:31.193 --> 00:01:36.576
It roared so loudly that Steve thought a train was driving through their kitchen.

25
00:01:37.356 --> 00:01:42.199
Dad had to shout at the top of his lungs to tell the family what to do.

26
00:01:42.219 --> 00:01:45.061
"Everyone! Go to the basement now!"

27
00:01:45.581 --> 00:01:46.281
he shouted.

28
00:01:46.762 --> 00:01:51.164
Dad turned off the electricity and Steve turned off the gas.

29
00:01:51.864 --> 00:01:54.346
Then the family hid in the basement.

30
00:01:55.506 --> 00:01:56.887
The noise grew louder and louder.

31
00:01:58.508 --> 00:02:00.249
Then the house started to shake.

32
00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:04.612
They could hear the glass smashing and wood breaking.

33
00:02:05.212 --> 00:02:06.493
It was terrifying.

34
00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:09.594
Steve and his sister started to cry.

35
00:02:09.614 --> 00:02:11.616
"What's going on?"

36
00:02:12.276 --> 00:02:13.116
Steve shouted.

37
00:02:13.136 --> 00:02:15.678
"The tornado is hitting our house!"

38
00:02:16.358 --> 00:02:17.259
Dad shouted.

39
00:02:17.279 --> 00:02:18.639
"Don't move!

40
00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:21.021
Cover your head with your hands."

41
00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:28.477
After a few terrible minutes, the sound quieted down and the house stopped shaking.

42
00:02:29.197 --> 00:02:33.139
Steve and his family carefully climbed out of their basement.

43
00:02:33.859 --> 00:02:35.920
Their house was a complete mess.

44
00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:42.843
All of the windows had been smashed to pieces, and things had been blown all over the house.

45
00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:46.985
Outside, things were just as bad.

46
00:02:47.645 --> 00:02:53.348
The family car was upside down, and most of their trees had been knocked down.

47
00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:57.222
Debris was scattered all over the neighborhood.

48
00:02:57.903 --> 00:02:59.484
Steve started to cry.

49
00:02:59.504 --> 00:03:04.528
"Everything we own is gone," cried Steve.

50
00:03:05.108 --> 00:03:09.111
But Steve's dad replied, "That's not true, Steve.

51
00:03:09.551 --> 00:03:13.594
We're all alive and safe, and that's what is most important."

52
00:03:17.177 --> 00:03:21.680
Tornadoes are very powerful and can cause great destruction.

53
00:03:22.628 --> 00:03:28.812
When warm, moist air collides with cold, dry air, the air does not mix well.

54
00:03:29.612 --> 00:03:34.615
If warm air gets trapped below the cold air, it tries to push itself up.

55
00:03:35.355 --> 00:03:40.338
As the warm air moves upward, it spins around extremely quickly.

56
00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:46.622
The mixing of cold air and warm air causes a thunderstorm.

57
00:03:47.442 --> 00:03:53.771
Usually the thunderstorm just dies out, but sometimes the air rotation is very strong.

58
00:03:54.552 --> 00:04:02.259
Most tornadoes are very small and don't cause much damage, but some tornadoes can be very dangerous.

59
00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:08.645
There are three kinds of tornadoes: weak, strong, and violent.

60
00:04:09.165 --> 00:04:15.411
A weak tornado will not hurt you if you are inside your house, but a strong tornado can

61
00:04:15.451 --> 00:04:16.752
be very harmful.

62
00:04:17.268 --> 00:04:22.613
However, if you are in the basement of your house, you will probably be okay.

63
00:04:23.413 --> 00:04:25.495
Violent tornadoes are the worst.

64
00:04:26.135 --> 00:04:27.777
They are the real killers.

65
00:04:28.537 --> 00:04:32.721
Even if you are in your basement, you may not be safe from one of them.

66
00:04:34.202 --> 00:04:37.385
The tornado that hit Steve's house was a strong one.

67
00:04:37.985 --> 00:04:42.549
The wind twisting inside it was about two hundred kilometers an hour.

68
00:04:43.009 --> 00:04:46.292
That is twice as fast as a car drives on the highway.

69
00:04:46.972 --> 00:04:53.935
Steve and his family are alive and safe today because they listened to the tornado warning and took

70
00:04:54.055 --> 00:04:55.696
refuge in their basement.

71
00:04:58.437 --> 00:05:06.221
After several weeks of hard work, Steve's family managed to repair their house and return to their usual

72
00:05:06.321 --> 00:05:11.863
life. But Steve never forgot the day when the tornado hit his house.
